From cff06234a5dd916cfc464b37a34e22e6c09c392f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 17:11:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0124 -- read-only HW-identity accessors (telemetry
 RUNMANIFEST)

WHY DOS NEEDS THIS: the card-identity values the cross-CPU QA matrix leans on
-- video VRAM size + the LFB-vs-banked decision, audio DMA-path + DSP version
-- are all computed inside SDL's own probe paths (GetVESAInfo, the mode-set LFB
guard, the SB16 DSP + BLASTER parse) and only ever reach <TAG>SDL.LOG. The
engine has no way to read them, so the telemetry RUNMANIFEST (nx-engine) cannot
record the hardware witness that makes each banked cell self-identifying.
SDL_DOSVesaDirectGetState exports framebuffer GEOMETRY, not the VRAM probe or
the SB identity.

Adds a new workspace-local public header include/SDL3/SDL_dosident.h with seven
read-only accessors over values SDL has ALREADY computed -- no new probing, no
I/O, no behaviour change, no per-frame cost; each returns a benign sentinel
(0 / false / -1) before its subsystem is up:
  Uint32 SDL_DOSVideoGetVRAMKB(void)            -- probed VRAM in KB
  bool   SDL_DOSVideoIsBankedMode(void)         -- resolved LFB-vs-banked decision
  bool   SDL_DOSAudioIsHighDMAPath(void)        -- RESOLVED path (16-high vs 8-low)
  bool   SDL_DOSAudioIsForced8Bit(void)         -- the force-8bit override lever
  int    SDL_DOSAudioGetDSPVersionMajor(void)   -- DSP major (-1 if unprobed)
  int    SDL_DOSAudioGetDSPVersionMinor(void)   -- DSP minor (-1 if unprobed)
  int    SDL_DOSAudioGetResolvedDMAChannel(void)-- channel in use (-1 if none)

The SB DMA path is kept as OUTCOME (IsHighDMAPath) + OVERRIDE (IsForced8Bit)
separate accessors, and CARD IDENTITY is recovered from the DSP version already
exposed -- SB16-class == SDL_DOSAudioGetDSPVersionMajor() >= 4 (the standard SB16
detection, and the very term in the soundblaster_is_sb16 expression). There is
deliberately NO "IsSB16" accessor: the round-2 X8 cell runs a genuine SB16 Vibra
with force-8bit=1, so a field with that name would report a real SB16 as
not-an-SB16 (if it returned the path) or read as the path when it did not (if it
returned identity). A wrong name is more expensive than a missing value -- a
missing value gets chased, a wrong one gets believed. Same lesson as the
binary_sha12 split earlier this round.

These are LIVE in-process reads, not stale echoed values, so consumers need no
provenance tag. Batched into the Tier-3 correctness binary so the telemetry set
does not cost a second Organya-cache re-render cycle. Per POST-BENCHMARK-PLAN.md
(nx slot 0294 wires against these).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
